by wachterjohannes at 2026-09-21T19:28:28Z

Thanks for working on this! Two things from the `--no-interaction` series (#1810 to #1826), then some smaller finds.

The answers live in properties again, set in `interact()` and read in `generate()`. That is exactly the shape we just removed from every other maker. PHP version, branch and database cannot be passed on the CLI at all. Make them options, let `interact()` only ask for what is missing, and let `generate()` read the input. That also collapses the duplicated logic in `buildProfile()`.

`--no-interaction` without `--platform` silently generates GitHub Actions. The platform is a fork in the output. I would fail and name the option, or guess only from an existing `.github/` or `.gitlab-ci.yml`.

Also worth a look: a rerun seems to overwrite a hand-edited CI file (`dependabot.yml` is guarded with `fileExists()`, the two CI files are not). Doctrine is only detected as `doctrine/orm`, so an unexpanded `symfony/orm-pack` gets a CI without a database, while the test pack is handled. And since no fixture has Doctrine, the database blocks of both templates are never generated in any test.

On scope that is already settled. One maintenance thought though: pinned actions and CI syntax age faster than PHP templates, so in a tagged release these files start aging on day one. Something to keep in mind for how often this needs a refresh.

